+## R3 request stop and effect accounting
+
+**I2. Stop before the next inference or dispatch.** NativeReAct produces exactly one action, calls its executor synchronously, appends the observation, then can invoke _generate again. Keep this loop. Under the existing ask lock tie the borrowed view, caller-thread subscription and original request-bound WorkLedger to this one composition. A validated action opens one transient expected-dispatch correlation UUID (a product ID, not an SDK ToolCall.id) with tool name and request/session/task. Capture original SDK START, END and TOOL_TIMEOUT using exact request binding, caller thread, expected action and tool. EventBus invokes callbacks synchronously but swallows callback exceptions; callbacks only record state. The generate decorator checks the latch *before calling its inner generate*, and the runner checks once more on return. Require exactly one successful matching END for the previous action and no compose adapter failure/timeout; exclude prerequisite records by phase, never by tool name. False END or timeout latches the original failure permanently. Unknown tools, permission denial or loop guard may produce no START/END; missing confirmation fails closed before another inner generation. Retain actual native observation from the SDK history when available and raw trace/ledger/normal-return tool_results, including actual false END metadata; absence of an SDK result/event is never filled with a synthetic result or start. Do not parse success from tool prose. A wire-valid but unsupported report thus receives one failed dispatch, zero write-intents, zero subsequent inference and CLI2. Whole-request no-write additionally requires no earlier effect.
+
+**I3. Two observable boundaries.** The installed tools/_stubs.py publishes START (tool, arguments, agent) before submitting the worker, then may publish TOOL_TIMEOUT (tool, timeout) after future.cancel() without knowing whether cancellation won; END contains tool/success/result/metadata. These events omit native ToolCall.id. Persist their real fields in the trace. Only a matching report START opens a request-local pending report; register its dispatch correlation UUID and bound candidate path from checked_path on the caller, or leave path unavailable if unsafe. This does not authorize a write or prove a worker started. WorkResearchWriteTool.run links its actual adapter call_id to that pending report in the captured ledger and validates ALL facts, sections and source bindings. It renders once, then calls the nested pre-bound WorkWriteTool. In the nested write branch only, after binding, path, mode and parameter checks and immediately before actual FileWriteTool.execute, record write-intent with original identities, resolved authorized path, outer report adapter call_id, file adapter call_id and dispatch UUID when present. Link this via the existing captured ledger's single outstanding report and private parent-report context on its pre-bound writer, never via public tool params. Preserve terminal SDK success/error under the same file call ID even on exceptions. Read branch and ordinary file tool path remain unchanged.
+
+Use the existing WorkLedger RLock for transient pending/intent and snapshots, keeping effect observations separate from terminal tool records. Never count a pending/intent observation as failed ToolResult, completed write or artifact. Store it in a separate bound diagnostic field in the response with a detached copy. On known synchronous validation/path rejection and false END (no timeout/intent/earlier effect), classify failed/CLI2. START alone followed by definitive normal rejection is not a possible write. On SDK failure after intent classify possible partial/truncation/commit. On timeout or outer loss with unresolved report START classify possible even if the worker marker is not yet visible. False END after TIMEOUT cannot clear uncertainty. Either possible case is needs_attention/CLI2, with the real cause and no verified artifact. Any committed write followed by a bad final similarly retains needs_attention, original call IDs/bytes and readback. On a success path require all regular readback gates. No SDK cancellation assertion, replay, rollback or durability work.
+
+Return one immutable response snapshot of the original ledger, including effects. A late worker still holds the old binding and ledger; never reuse either for another submission or change the returned status. For independent failed-artifact readback prefer the real successful bound write; without one, use only a checked original path from the write-intent or unresolved dispatch with matching request/task/session. Revalidate checked_path/reparse rules on reopen. Record observation time and actual bytes/hash or absence/unreadability, with unknown outcome when causal effect is unverified. Never open an unchecked path or infer cancellation or permanent absence from a single read. Full support stays in ledger; successful report observations to the model contain only path, cited IDs and bounded completion metadata, not the echoed report/support payload. No worker manager, new executor, durable ledger, background poller or cancellation/retry engine.
